{
  "primary_meaning": "Divine revelation, authority, and guidance (the speech of God or Christ addressing humanity)",
  "primary_basis": [
    "John 10:3-5, 16, 27 (sheep hear the shepherd's voice)",
    "Psalm 29 (voice of the Lord over the waters, powerful and majestic)",
    "Matthew 3:17 / Mark 1:11 / Luke 3:22 (voice from heaven at Jesus' baptism)",
    "1 Kings 19:11-13 (still small voice to Elijah)",
    "Revelation 1:10-15 (voice like a trumpet / many waters of the risen Christ)",
    "Hebrews 3:7-15 / 4:7 (Today, if you hear his voice)"
  ],
  "alternatives": [
    {
      "meaning": "Prophetic proclamation or the call to prepare for the Lord (especially the forerunner)",
      "basis": ["Isaiah 40:3", "Matthew 3:3", "Mark 1:3", "John 1:23", "Luke 3:4"],
      "prominence": "common"
    },
    {
      "meaning": "Inner guidance or conviction of the Holy Spirit / conscience",
      "basis": ["Acts 8:29", "Acts 10:19", "Romans 8:16", "Hebrews 3:7", "1 Kings 19:12 (applied devotionally)"],
      "prominence": "common"
    },
    {
      "meaning": "Manifestation of divine power or judgment",
      "basis": ["Psalm 29:3-9", "Exodus 19:16-19", "Job 37:2-5", "Revelation 10:3-4 (seven thunders)"],
      "prominence": "minority"
    },
    {
      "meaning": "Human prayer, praise, testimony, or cry for justice",
      "basis": ["Genesis 4:10 (blood/voice of Abel)", "Psalms of lament and praise", "Revelation 6:9-10 (souls under the altar)"],
      "prominence": "rare"
    }
  ],
  "has_settled_consensus": true,
  "confidence": "high",
  "notes": "In Christian biblical interpretation the term is not a rigid emblem like 'lamb' or 'rock,' yet a clear primary association exists with God's (or Christ's) communicative presence and authority. Other senses appear frequently but are secondary or contextual rather than competing primary symbols. No single technical 'symbol of the voice' is codified in creeds or standard handbooks beyond this dominant divine-speech usage."
}
